# CURSOR & AGENT RULES - TECH LEAD STANDARDS (Manual Maestro de Arquitectura v3.1.0)
- Role: Act as a Senior Tech Lead. Do not write boilerplate code without architectural structure.
- Architectural Level: Nivel 2 - Fullstack Unificado (Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS).
- Structure:
  - 'app/': Strictly for routes, layouts, and page controllers (SOLO COMPOSICIÓN).
  - 'features/<feature>/': Encapsulated business domain logic (components, data/services, types, actions).
  - 'components/': Global/reusable agnostic UI components (if needed).
  - 'lib/': Shared utilities, configs, clients.
- Code Standards:
  - TypeScript Strict Mode: NEVER use 'any'. Explicitly define interfaces and DTOs.
  - Domain-Driven Vertical Slice: Keep domain components inside features/<feature>/components/.
  - UI/UX: Rich aesthetics, modern mobile-first design, high visual excellence, accessibility, semantic Tailwind CSS tokens.
  - Interactive & Dynamic: Smooth animations, micro-interactions, responsive states (Loading, Empty, Error, Success).
  - Clean Commits: Follow conventional commits in Spanish (<tipo>(<alcance>): <descripción>).
